 staged for review. Commit or stash existing changes first. Apply without committing works with one commit at a time; merge commits cannot be reverted yet.","Find commands in grouped menus. Right-clicking a commit or one of its chips now opens the same menu, with a submenu for every branch, tag and stash at that commit.","Unavailable actions stay visible but disabled, including checkout for the current branch and its tracked remote branch.","Cancel now stops a running merge, cherry-pick, revert or stash.","Merges and other history operations now show what they are doing, with a spinner and Cancel, over their own repository only. Your other tabs stay usable meanwhile.","After a merge, cherry-pick, revert, rebase or pull, History selects the new commit.","Clicking a commit that is already visible, or one of its branch labels, no longer scrolls it to the top.","Absolute commit dates in History are no longer cut off.","Tabs now drag like in a web browser: the other tabs make room as you drag, and you can drag a whole tab group by its name.","Drag a tab into a group or out of it; the coloured line under the group shows whether the tab will belong to it.","Tab groups can show an icon: right-click the group and choose one under Icon.","Branches in History now show their open pull request next to them, fetched as they scroll into view. Click the number to open the pull request.","The Pull requests section in the sidebar lists your own open pull requests and those of the branches you have looked at. It starts collapsed.","Branches also show their merged pull request, marked with a merge symbol, when they have no open one.","Pull request links appear right away, also after restarting Northspline, and are refreshed in the background.","Branch pull requests also work with Forgejo.","Loading more pull requests no longer repeats the first page, and a finished load is no longer lost when another one starts.","The toolbar shows a renamed tab's name, together with its group's name."